title Account Authentication and Lockout\nNFR-002, FR-002 (conditional draft: OC-1 open)

[*] --> Unlocked : register

Unlocked : failedLoginCount 0 to 4
Unlocked : lockedUntil is empty or expired
Unlocked : --
Unlocked : correct password / count = 0; lock cleared; session created
Unlocked : wrong password [count below 4] / count + 1; generic message

Locked : failedLoginCount = 5
Locked : now is before lockedUntil
Locked : --
Locked : any attempt, even with the correct password /
Locked :    refused before any password check; not counted;
Locked :    lock not extended; "temporarily locked" message

Unlocked --> Locked : wrong password [count = 4] / count = 5;\nlockedUntil = now + 5 minutes; generic message
Locked --> Unlocked : now reaches lockedUntil (exactly +5:00) /\ncount restarts from 0 at the next attempt

legend bottom left
  State is persisted, so a restart cannot clear it. Time comes from an injected Clock, so tests can check +4:59 and +5:00.
  Lock state is derived from failedLoginCount and lockedUntil; no separate status is stored.
  "Consecutive" counts per account, across sessions and restarts. Only a success or a lock expiry clears the count.
  Unknown usernames have no state; they get the same generic message as a wrong password.
endlegend

@enduml
